{
    "background_story": "Reese was a classically trained pianist with a passion for Russian composers. Among her favorites was Bed\u0159ich Smetana, whose majestic works transported her to a world of elegance and refinement. As a child, Reese would spend hours listening to her mother's old records, mesmerized by the lush melodies of Smetana's 'M\u00e1 Vlast'. As she grew older, Reese became determined to master the composer's most challenging pieces. Her dedication paid off when she was invited to perform Smetana's 'Piano Trio in G minor' at a prestigious music festival in Prague. The crowd was enchanted by her nuanced interpretation, and Reese felt a deep connection to the city where Smetana's music was born. From that moment on, she was known as the 'Smetana virtuoso', and her love for the composer's music continued to inspire her performances.",
